reator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Manash Pratim Gohain</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135091554,imgsize-52326.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Monsoon's gone, El Niño isn't: Why India's weather worries are far from over]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/monsoons-gone-el-nio-isnt-why-indias-weather-worries-are-far-from-over/articleshow/135090741.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135090741.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[El Niño is increasingly influencing global weather patterns including agriculture and temperatures in India. Current forecasts predict a warmer winter as El Niño intensifies, which could affect agriculture adversely. Recent monsoon rainfall deficits raise concerns regarding water resources and crop yields moving forward. Different regions may experience varying extremes from drought to flooding in the coming months due to this phenomenon.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/monsoons-gone-el-nio-isnt-why-indias-weather-worries-are-far-from-over/articleshow/135090741.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/monsoons-gone-el-nio-isnt-why-indias-weather-worries-are-far-from-over/articleshow/135090741.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T16:53:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aryan Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135090828,imgsize-79298.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘I'm not a travel agent’: Shashi Tharoor when asked about Rahul Gandhi's foreign trip]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/im-not-a-travel-agent-shashi-tharoor-when-asked-about-rahul-gandhis-foreign-trip/articleshow/135090753.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" sty